1.	Say to the king who entreats the gods fervently and, serving the gods, prepares the food offerings; repeat to the one elevated in stature who has the ability to give advice and counsel, the merciful one who makes the Land feel content -- this is what @wPN{Inim-Enlila} the scribe, son of @wPN{Suen-palil}, your servant, says: 
8.	I do not know my punishment: my punishment has not been considered yet. 
9.	I am devoured by sorrow at the fate of the captive (?) families. 
10.	Let my bones not be carried off by water to a foreign city. 
1.	@gap{1 line fragmentary} @note{may not be part of this composition} @gap{unknown no. of lines missing}
